num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Allocation**\n\n- **Fund level:** The fund pays a single unitary management fee to the platform adviser under the advisory agreement. The adviser, in turn, pays ordinary operating expenses: custody, administration, transfer agency, fund accounting, legal, audit, index licensing, and trustee fees. Contractually excluded expenses remain fund costs. These typically include interest, taxes, brokerage commissions, acquired-fund fees, 12b-1 fees, and litigation or extraordinary expenses.\n\n- **Adviser and sponsor level:** Under a separate agreement, the brand sponsor assumes the fund's expenses. The adviser retains a negotiated portion of the fee, often with a minimum. The sponsor keeps the remainder after paying expenses and covers any shortfall. Splits vary by contract; there is no standard percentage.\n\n**Continuing obligation**\n\nThe adviser remains contractually liable to the fund for covered expenses. The sponsor's assumption is a private adviser–sponsor arrangement. It neither releases the adviser nor shifts cost risk to shareholders.","ttft_ms":2182,"type":"result","duration_ms":4809,"uuid":"94aa2bb4-76a0-4951-bb87-22ddabb61e2a","ttft_stream_ms":1823,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":1823,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
